---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const description =
  'Lodestone Consulting is grounded in active product development across regulated AI — nuclear V&V tooling, medical records processing, institutional-memory systems, document-generation engines. Led by Ryan Hanson, Corvallis, Oregon.';
---
<Base title="About" description={description}>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span class="here">About</span></p>
      <h1>Methodology from doing the work.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Lodestone Consulting is grounded in active product development across regulated AI — not theorizing about it from the outside.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap two-col">
      <div>
        <h2>About</h2>
        <p>
          The methodology comes from building real systems: LLM tooling for nuclear verification &amp; validation,
          medical records processing, institutional-memory platforms, long-form document-generation engines. When
          we recommend an approach, it's grounded in implementation reality, not a slide. Led by
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ryan-hanson-0a766b30/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ryan Hanson</a>
          out of Corvallis, Oregon — remote-first, travel available.
        </p>
        <p>
          Most consulting in this space falls into one of two camps: management consultants who write decks but don't
          build, or technical consultants who build but don't think about the institution. We do both. The result is
          institutional artifacts — methodologies, audits, ConOps, decision frameworks — that hold up under scrutiny
          and stay useful after we leave.
        </p>
        <h2 style="margin-top:1.6em;">Where we've worked</h2>
        <ul class="value-list">
          <li><strong>Healthcare &amp; medical AI</strong><span>HIPAA architecture, PHI handling, EHR integration, de-identification pipelines.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Nuclear energy</strong><span>Airgapped deployment, NRC cyber security, V&amp;V tooling, safety-class workflows.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Enterprise software</strong><span>Document processing, workflow automation, knowledge management.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Creative &amp; media</strong><span>Co-narrative AI systems and content-generation pipelines.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <aside class="meta">
        <h3>Principles</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Discretion.</strong> Client engagements stay private unless you authorize otherwise. No case studies, no client lists, no name-drops.</li>
          <li><strong>Durable artifacts.</strong> Documents your successor can use, not your hire-of-the-month.</li>
          <li><strong>Ship, not just advise.</strong> Decks alone don't change institutions.</li>
          <li><strong>Vendor-neutral.</strong> No partnerships, no referral fees, no preferred vendors.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest about scope.</strong> Change orders before work, not invoices after.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Work with someone who's built the thing.</h2>
      <p>If your problem lives where the institution meets the technical detail, that's exactly the seam we work.</p>
      <p class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn">Start a conversation</a>
        <a href="/services" class="btn-ghost">Browse services</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
